r a fixed window of 60 seconds.\",\n      \"line\": 3,\n      \"span\": \"Requests are counted against the credential that presented them, over a fixed window of 60 seconds\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Requests are never counted against a connection.\",\n      \"line\": 3,\n      \"span\": \"never against a connection\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Opening a second socket buys a caller nothing.\",\n      \"line\": 3,\n      \"span\": \"Opening a second socket therefore buys a caller nothing\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A client spread across multiple worker processes is throttled at exactly the point a single process would have been.\",\n      \"line\": 3,\n      \"span\": \"a client spread across multiple worker processes is throttled at exactly the point a single process would have been\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The default allowance is 100 requests in a window.\",\n      \"line\": 5,\n      \"span\": \"The default allowance is 100 requests in a window\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A credential marked for batch work is allowed 1000 in the same window.\",\n      \"line\": 5,\n      \"span\": \"A credential marked for batch work is allowed 1000 in the same window\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A refusal is the platform declining to spend capacity that has already been promised to somebody else.\",\n      \"line\": 5,\n      \"span\": \"It is the platform declining to spend capacity that has already been promised to somebody else\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Callers that retry immediately are the largest single reason the cap is there at all.\",\n      \"line\": 5,\n      \"span\": \"Callers that retry immediately are the largest single reason the cap is there at all\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The refusal carries a Retry-After header.\",\n      \"line\": 9,\n      \"span\": \"The refusal carries a Retry-After header\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The value of the Retry-After header is a whole number of seconds to wait.\",\n      \"line\": 9,\n      \"span\": \"Its value is a whole number of seconds to wait\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The gateway keeps no memory of who backed off politely.\",\n      \"line\": 9,\n      \"span\": \"The gateway keeps no memory of who backed off politely\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Waiting longer than the header asks earns a caller no credit at all.\",\n      \"line\": 9,\n      \"span\": \"waiting longer than the header asks earns a caller no credit at all\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The body of the refusal is JSON.\",\n      \"line\": 11,\n      \"span\": \"The body of the refusal is JSON\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The body names what the gateway calls the window it counted in.\",\n      \"line\": 11,\n      \"span\": \"it names what the gateway calls the \\\"window\\\" it counted in\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The body names the cap and the tier.\",\n      \"line\": 11,\n      \"span\": \"It names the cap and the tier as well\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A caller that parses the body to compute its own wait is doing the same arithmetic twice.\",\n      \"line\": 11,\n      \"span\": \"a caller that parses the body to compute its own wait is doing the same arithmetic twice\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The gateway has already done the arithmetic with information the caller does not have.\",\n      \"line\": 17,\n      \"span\": \"The gateway has already done that arithmetic, with information the caller does not have\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The gateway does the same on the 503 path.\",\n      \"line\": 17,\n      \"span\": \"it does the same on the 503 path\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A wait derived on the client side is a guess about a counter the client cannot see.\",\n      \"line\": 17,\n      \"span\": \"A wait derived on the client side is a guess about a counter it cannot see\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A 200 response wants nothing.\",\n      \"line\": 19,\n      \"span\": \"A 200 wants nothing\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A 429 response wants the stated wait.\",\n      \"line\": 19,\n      \"span\": \"a 429 wants the stated wait\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A 500 may be retried once that wait has passed.\",\n      \"line\": 19,\n      \"span\": \"a 500 may be retried once that wait has passed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A 503 is the overload path.\",\n      \"line\": 19,\n      \"span\": \"a 503 is the overload path\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A client that folds every non-success into one branch will retry hardest during exactly the incident the cap was installed to survive.\",\n      \"line\": 19,\n      \"span\": \"A client that folds every non-success into one branch will retry hardest during exactly the incident the cap was installed to survive\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A batch credential is allowed fifty times the default allowance.\",\n      \"line\": 21,\n      \"span\": \"A batch credential is allowed fifty times the default allowance\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A batch credential allowance is measured over exactly the same window.\",\n      \"line\": 21,\n      \"span\": \"it is measured over exactly the same window\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The tier is set on the credential when it is issued.\",\n      \"line\": 21,\n      \"span\": \"The tier is set on the credential when it is issued\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The tier cannot be asked for per call.\",\n      \"line\": 21,\n      \"span\": \"cannot be asked for per call\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Nothing else about the two tiers differs in any way.\",\n      \"line\": 21,\n      \"span\": \"Nothing else about the two tiers differs in any way\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Nobody at the far end will assemble the argument on the caller's behalf.\",\n      \"line\": 23,\n      \"span\": \"nobody at the far end will assemble that argument on its behalf\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A credential may be suspended.\",\n      \"line\": 27,\n      \"span\": \"A credential may be suspended\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A route may be closed for maintenance.\",\n      \"line\": 27,\n      \"span\": \"a route may be closed for maintenance\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A body may exceed the 5 megabyte limit.\",\n      \"line\": 27,\n      \"span\": \"a body may exceed the 5 megabyte limit\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"None of those three clears itself by waiting for a stated number of seconds.\",\n      \"line\": 27,\n      \"span\": \"None of those three clears itself by waiting for a stated number of seconds\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A loop that waits and retries against a suspended credential spends its whole budget without ever reaching the service.\",\n      \"line\": 29,\n      \"span\": \"A loop that waits and retries against a suspended credential spends its whole budget without ever reaching the service\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The log afterwards shows nothing at all except a long run of refusals.\",\n      \"line\": 29,\n      \"span\": \"the log afterwards shows nothing at all except a long run of refusals\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Reading the status code rather than the class it belongs to is what separates the two cases.\",\n      \"line\": 29,\n      \"span\": \"Reading the status code rather than the class it belongs to is what separates the two cases\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Reading the status code rather than the class it belongs to costs one comparison.\",\n      \"line\": 29,\n      \"span\": \"it costs one comparison\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The platform team looks at whether the load is smooth or bursty.\",\n      \"line\": 33,\n      \"span\": \"The platform team looks at whether the load is smooth or bursty\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A burst is cheaper to smooth than it is to serve at its peak.\",\n      \"line\": 33,\n      \"span\": \"a burst is cheaper to smooth than it is to serve at its peak\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A caller that can move half its work to a quieter hour usually gets what it needs without any change to the cap at all.\",\n      \"line\": 33,\n      \"span\": \"A caller that can move half its work to a quieter hour usually gets what it needs without any change to the cap at all\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Everyone prefers the outcome where callers get what they need without the cap being changed.\",\n      \"line\": 33,\n      \"span\": \"which is the outcome everyone prefers\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Requests reach the platform team through the usual channel.\",\n      \"line\": 35,\n      \"span\": \"Requests reach the platform team through the usual channel\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Requests are answered within two working days.\",\n      \"line\": 35,\n      \"span\": \"they are answered within two working days\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"There is no expedited path.\",\n      \"line\": 35,\n      \"span\": \"There is no expedited path\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"There is no exception list.\",\n      \"line\": 35,\n      \"span\": \"There is no exception list\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":127050,"type":"result","duration_ms":148904,"uuid":"d93cd2b0-0dd3-494a-aeb1-051efa0ef231","ttft_stream_ms":892,"time_to_request_ms":96,"first_content_frame_ms":893,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
